WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
Open the Sikh scripture, and you will
find hymns by a Muslim Sufi named Sheikh

2
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:05.700
Farid.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.940
Beside them are hymns by
saints from Hindu backgrounds,

4
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.490
such as Ravidas and Namdev.

5
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:17.500
Guru Nanak, the first Sikh Guru, was
born in 1469 to a Hindu family and worked

6
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.260
for a Muslim official.

7
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:24.830
So if Sikhism grew up among both
faiths, why do Sikhs say it is neither?

8
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll
travel to Punjab around 1500,

9
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.030
where Muslim rulers governed
mostly Hindu villages.

10
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.090
Then you'll follow the Gurus
and the Mughal emperors,

11
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.430
all the way to the Khalsa in 1699.

12
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.730
Your mission: find out why Sikhs say
their faith is neither Hindu nor Muslim.
